# Accessibility Audit

## Checklist

- All non-text content has a text alternative (alt, accessibilityLabel, contentDescription).
- Decorative images hidden from assistive tech.
- Colour not the only means of conveying information.
- Colour contrast ≥ 4.5:1 normal text, ≥ 3:1 large text and UI components.
- All interactive elements keyboard/focus reachable with visible focus indicator.
- No keyboard traps. Focus order is logical.
- Touch targets ≥ 44×44pt (iOS), 48×48dp (Android), 44×44px (web).
- Form inputs have programmatically associated labels (not just placeholders).
- Error messages identify the field and describe the fix.
- Semantic HTML: `<button>` not `<div onClick>`, correct heading hierarchy.
- ARIA used only when native semantics are insufficient; no conflicting ARIA.
- Focus managed on modal open/close and route change.
- Dynamic content announced via `aria-live` or platform equivalent.

## Output Format

```markdown
## Accessibility Findings

**[P0]** `path/file.ext:line` - Title
Barrier description and fix.

## Summary
WCAG level assessed and priority fixes.
```
